      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the smallest positive integer \\( B \\) such that every prime factor of Alice's number \\( A = 24 \\) is also a prime factor of \\( B \\).\n\nFirst, we find the prime factorization of \\( A = 24 \\):\n\\[\n24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1\n\\]\nThis means the prime factors of \\( A \\) are \\( 2 \\) and \\( 3 \\).\n\nFor \\( B \\) to satisfy the condition, \\( B \\) must include \\( 2 \\) and \\( 3 \\) as its prime factors. The smallest number that includes both \\( 2 \\) and \\( 3 \\) as prime factors is their product:\n\\[\nB = 2 \\times 3 = 6\n\\]\n\nWe need to verify that \\( B = 6 \\) meets the criteria:\n- The prime factors of \\( 6 \\) are \\( 2 \\) and \\( 3 \\).\n- Both prime factors \\( 2 \\) and \\( 3 \\) are also factors of \\( 24 \\).\n\nSince the conditions are satisfied, the smallest possible number that Bob could have is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
